---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "sec-install", label: "01 INSTALL" },
  { id: "sec-first", label: "02 FIRST EVIDENCE → SHIP-CHECK" },
  { id: "sec-legacy", label: "03 LEGACY PIPELINE (V0.1)" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started — Kineti"
  description="Install Kineti and run your first evidence → ship-check → verify. Default path is init, evidence, ship-check, receipt, verify."
  active="getting-started"
  {toc}
>
  <!-- 1. INSTALL -->
  <section id="sec-install" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-install" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-install" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">01</span>INSTALL</h2>
    <pre class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="font-bold text-fg">curl -fsSL https://getkineti.com/install.sh | sh</span></code></pre>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Pin a version (optional):</p>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="font-bold text-fg">curl -fsSL https://getkineti.com/install.sh | sh -s v0.2.0</span></code></pre>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Supported platforms: <strong class="text-fg">macOS</strong> (Apple silicon &amp; Intel) and
      <strong class="text-fg">Linux</strong> x64/arm64 — Linux installs the zero-dependency musl-static build
      when available. The script checks every download against the release's
      <code class="text-accent">SHA256SUMS</code> before executing it and never asks for sudo.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Install location, in order: <code class="text-accent">$KINETI_INSTALL_DIR</code> →
      <code class="text-accent">/usr/local/bin</code> (only if writable) →
      <code class="text-accent">~/.local/bin</code> → <code class="text-accent">~/.cargo/bin</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Or from source:</p>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="font-bold text-fg">cargo install --git https://github.com/therawlogs/kineti</span></code></pre>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      No sudo. Verify after install from the release page:
      <code class="text-accent">sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS</code>.
    </p>
    <h3 class="mt-8 text-sm font-bold text-fg">Uninstall</h3>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="font-bold text-fg">rm -f /usr/local/bin/kineti "$HOME/.local/bin/kineti" "$HOME/.cargo/bin/kineti"</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">rm -rf ~/.kineti/auth</span>          <span class="text-muted"># stored login tokens</span>
<span class="text-muted"># per project where you ran kineti init:</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">rm -rf .kineti kineti.toml</span></code></pre>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. FIRST EVIDENCE → SHIP-CHECK -->
  <section id="sec-first" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-first" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-first" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">02</span>FIRST EVIDENCE → SHIP-CHECK</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Default path is <code class="text-accent">init → evidence → ship-check → receipt → verify</code>. Works
      with any agent — Claude, Cursor, Grok, or a shell script.
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti init</span>                                   <span class="text-muted"># scaffold .kineti/ + kineti.toml</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti evidence --cmd "cargo test"</span>          <span class="text-muted"># or npm test / ./greeting.sh — binds result to file hashes</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti ship-check</span>                             <span class="text-muted"># red if files moved since the proof</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti receipt</span>                                <span class="text-muted"># hash-chained run summary</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti verify --all</span>                           <span class="text-muted"># full DAG check</span></code></pre>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p><strong class="text-fg">`kineti evidence --cmd "your test"`</strong> runs your verify command and writes <code class="text-accent">.kineti/evidence.json</code> with <code class="text-soft">passed</code>, <code class="text-soft">fingerprint</code> (hash of tracked files), and <code class="text-soft">at</code>. Edit a file — fingerprint flips stale and <code class="text-accent">ship-check</code> refuses.</p>
      <p><strong class="text-fg">`kineti ship-check`</strong> is what you put in CI required checks. Exit <code class="text-soft">0</code> fresh, <code class="text-soft">1</code> stale/failed, <code class="text-soft">2</code> missing proof.</p>
      <p><strong class="text-fg">Spend cap:</strong> set <code class="text-accent">[limits].global_usd</code> in <code class="text-accent">kineti.toml</code> or pass <code class="text-accent">--cap</code> to a command. Crossing settled spend halts the run; only a human <code class="text-accent">.kineti/spend.reset</code> file resumes (see <a href="/docs/receipt" class="text-accent hover:underline">Receipt</a>).</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Next: <a href="/docs/ci" class="text-accent hover:underline">CI</a> ·
      <a href="/docs/commands" class="text-accent hover:underline">Commands</a> ·
      <a href="/docs/receipt" class="text-accent hover:underline">Receipt</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. LEGACY PIPELINE -->
  <section id="sec-legacy" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-legacy" class="scroll-mt-20 py-10">
    <h2 id="h-legacy" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">03</span>LEGACY PIPELINE (V0.1)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <code class="text-accent">kineti run --goal ...</code>, <code class="text-accent">resume</code>, <code class="text-accent">task</code> and swarm flags are frozen on tag <code class="text-accent">v0.1.0</code>. They still work but are hidden from default help. Use <code class="text-accent">kineti run --help</code> to see them, or read <a href="https://github.com/therawlogs/kineti/blob/main/docs/v0.1.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">docs/v0.1.md</a> on GitHub. See also <a href="/docs/swarm" class="text-accent hover:underline">v0.1 swarm</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <code class="text-accent">kineti serve</code> is the local ledger daemon (<code class="text-soft">.kineti/kineti.sock</code> 0600). Hosted gateway + dashboard is a separate service, not part of the OSS binary.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
